      "title": "Canary Release Failure: Feature Flags Not Applying Due to Load Balancer Stale Configs",
      "content_summary": "Troubleshooting steps for canary deployments where feature flags fail to apply or cause breaking changes due to stale Load Balancer configurations and incomplete rollbacks.",
      "content_body": "When a canary release fails to apply feature flags, check if the Load Balancer is routing traffic to the previous version due to a stale configuration cache. This often happens if an incomplete rollback left the LB pointing to deprecated Secret Store endpoints, causing version incompatibilities. To resolve this, manually force a full rollback of the Load Balancer configuration to the known stable state before re-attempting the deployment. If the issue persists after a clean rollback, escalate to Engineering to verify the Secret Store rotation policy aligns with the new release candidate."
